-- Conditions, so that a turn past the easy rounds asks for more than one thing.
--
-- The whole object catalogue was one target at a time, which stopped being a
-- hunt once a player knew their own room. From here:
--
--   easy    one thing, exactly as before
--   medium  two things held in the same frame
--   hard    a rarer pair, three things, or three of the same
--
-- Nothing is retired: every quest that used to be medium or hard is still drawn,
-- it is just an easy round now, which also makes rounds 1-2 far less repetitive.
--
-- The requirement rides in `validator_config` rather than a new column, because
-- that column already reaches both the vision service and the browser untouched
-- by the RPC and the PostgREST select in between. `targetClasses` is the list
-- that must be in shot at once - a class repeated in it is how "two of these"
-- is written - and `targetLabels` names each one for the screen. `target_class`
-- stays set to the first of them, which is what the table check and the
-- background-avoidance ordering in prepare_turn read.

update public.quests
set difficulty = 'easy'
where kind in ('object', 'color') and difficulty <> 'easy';

-- Holding two things in one frame is the difficulty. Asking for the same 0.55
-- per-object confidence on top of that would lose fair attempts to one weak
-- reading, so each object is judged a little more leniently than a solo one.
